# The build context is sent to the Docker daemon before any layer is built, so a secret
# that is not COPYed into the image is still a secret sent over a socket and cached on a
# build host. INV-2 says no secret in a Docker image layer; this file keeps them out of
# the context as well.
#
# The Dockerfile only needs `pyproject.toml`, `uv.lock`, `src/` and its own base layers.

# VCS and CI
.git
.github

# Location configuration and secrets. `cameras.yml` holds substituted RTSP credentials;
# `.env` holds the credentials themselves.
.env
.env.*
config

# State and generated footage (INV-4: it lives on the host, never in an image)
data
dev-synthetic/data
dev-synthetic/fixture
dev-synthetic/frigate

# Development-only and throwaway harnesses
.venv
spike
dev-synthetic
tests
docs

# Tool caches
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
.uv-cache

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
.vscode

# Files not needed by the build
*.md
.gitignore
.pre-commit-config.yaml
compose.yml
install.sh
Dockerfile.dockerignore
